WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.740
Gamora from Guardians of the Galaxy knows
better than anyone else that parents just

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.020
don't understand — especially when they're
power-hungry madmen like Thanos who aren't

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.090
your real dad anyway.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.040
"I hope they remember you."

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.830
After ten years and 18 movies, Marvel Studios
finally pulled the trigger on having the Mad

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.580
Titan Thanos go toe-to-toe with the Avengers.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.089
But while everyone knows the Eternal's main
mission is to acquire all six stones for the

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:29.060
Infinity Gauntlet, a big part of that mission
revolves around his adopted daughter, Gamora.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.099
But how did this relationship begin in the
first place?

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:35.520
It changes depending on whether you're talking
about the Marvel Cinematic Universe or the

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.530
comic books, and also depending on which comic
you're reading — but the general skeleton

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.330
of their relationship remains the same no
matter what.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.600
Forget the finer details — this is all the
stuff you need to know about the relationship

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.530
between Thanos and Gamora.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:53.850
As established in the comics, Gamora is the
last surviving member of a pacifist race called

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.040
the Zen-Whoberis— or Zehoberei, as they
say it in the MCU.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.120
When she was a young girl, her people were
completely wiped out by a powerful invading

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.120
force.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.330
Afterwards, Thanos discovered her alive and
decided to adopt her, seeing great potential

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.900
in her as a deadly warrior.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.540
On the surface, that's pretty selfish — but
in an accidental fashion, it's also sort of

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.540
nice.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.080
That act of compassion for the sake of violence
in the midst of utter destruction would do

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.780
a lot to warp Gamora's developing mind in
the comic canon — but in the movies, it's

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.030
so much worse.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.940
In Gamora's comic origins, it was the evil
Magus and his Grand Inquisitors who destroyed

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:29.940
her race.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.760
But in the movies, it's established that Thanos
himself is the one who exterminated her folks,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.560
giving their relationship an intense and complex
twist with an icky undercurrent of emotional

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:40.560
abuse.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.210
Over the course of her childhood and adolescence,
Thanos was a stern disciplinarian of a father

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.840
who only occasionally betrayed his compassion
for his ward, and the harsh upbringing hardened

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.240
Gamora into exactly the sort of warrior Thanos
wanted her to be.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.920
But in spite of his goals of galactic domination
and mass murder, he's not 100% evil.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.490
Regardless of everything else, Thanos does
love his adopted daughter in his own weird

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.490
way.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.149
While he's violent and harsh to Gamora, he's
flat-out murderous to anyone who hurts her.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:15.060
The ninth issue of Warlock and the Infinity
Watch sees Gamora get attacked by a group

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.310
of violent crooks who outnumber and outmatch
her.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:23.640
While she was saved by Thanos, it was only
after the gang had already brutally beat her.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.080
Her body broken, Thanos demonstrated his peculiar
compassion by nursing her back to health,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:34.670
making her better, stronger, and faster than
she was before, replacing her entire skeleton,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:38.730
and enhancing her reflexes, respiratory system,
and physical strength.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.740
He also removed her tear ducts, so that the
young woman with the unspeakably hard life

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.800
would never know sorrow again, which may not
be how that works, on any level, but says

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.140
a lot about Thanos' mindset.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.740
Gamora stayed a ward of Thanos into adulthood,
sticking by her guardian's side until she

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.740
discovered Thanos' genocidal ambitions, which
he intends to realize with the full power

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:02.300
of the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.420
That realization was all the inspiration she
needed to turn against the Titan.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.510
Once she realized that her adopted father's
obsession with death on a massive scale was

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:15.790
the real deal, she set out on her own, finally
able to develop her own moral compass separate

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.560
from Thanos, the Worst Dad Ever.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.940
No spoilers here, but a major aspect of Avengers:
Infinity War revolves around Thanos' genuine

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.459
love for Gamora, giving the Death-obsessed
Titan a disarming amount of emotional complexity.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:33.670
But that compassion is outweighed by almost
everything else Thanos does, leaving Gamora

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:38.580
with no choice but to stand against the man
who raised her, and made her who she is.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.910
That should catch you up on just about everything
you need to know about Thanos and Gamora's

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:43.910
relationship.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.390
See where it all leads in the certified-fresh
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.390
Thanks for watching!

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.730
